  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14197487/assets/3123021ea5734c0ff2e8edcb716245b603de6f9dde7ebf0d367e1eeb8383bdf8.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-6,0].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $3$ and $10$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-6,0]$ given that $f(-6)=2.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
